skill: HTML and CSS

@ HTML Structure | B
Which tag defines the main, largest heading of a page?
= <h1>
- <h6>
- <head>
- <title>
? <h1> is the top-level heading. <title> sets the browser tab text and <head> holds metadata.

@ HTML Structure | B
Which attribute provides alternative text for an image?
= alt
- title
- src
- caption
? alt text is read by screen readers and shown when the image cannot load.

@ HTML Structure | B
Which tag creates an unordered (bulleted) list?
= <ul>
- <ol>
- <li>
- <dl>
? <ul> holds bullet items and <ol> holds numbered items. <li> is a list item.

@ HTML Structure | I
Which HTML5 element represents a section of navigation links?
= <nav>
- <menu-links>
- <links>
- <navigate>
? <nav> is a semantic element that helps accessibility and search engines understand the page.

@ Forms and Semantics | I
Which input type shows typed characters as dots?
= password
- hidden
- secret
- text-mask
? <input type="password"> masks the characters the user types.

@ Forms and Semantics | I
Which attribute makes a form field mandatory?
= required
- mandatory
- validate
- needed
? The required attribute lets the browser block submission when the field is empty.

@ CSS Selectors | B
Which selector targets the element with the id main?
= #main
- .main
- main
- *main
? # selects by id and . selects by class.

@ CSS Selectors | I
Which selector targets all p elements that are descendants of a div?
= div p
- div + p
- p div
- div, p
? A space is the descendant combinator. div > p would match only direct children.

@ CSS Selectors | I
Which has the higher specificity in CSS?
= An id selector
- A class selector
- An element selector
- They have equal specificity
? Specificity order from highest to lowest is inline style, id, class, element.

@ Box Model and Layout | I
With box-sizing: border-box, the width property includes:
= Content, padding and border
- Content only
- Content and margin
- Margin only
? border-box makes sizing more predictable because padding and border do not add to the declared width.

@ Box Model and Layout | I
Which declaration positions an element relative to its nearest positioned ancestor?
= position: absolute
- position: static
- float: none
- display: block
? Absolutely positioned elements are placed using top, right, bottom and left relative to the nearest ancestor that is not static.

@ Box Model and Layout | A
What does z-index control?
= The stacking order of positioned elements
- The zoom level of a page
- The transparency of an element
- The font size
? Higher z-index values appear in front of lower values for positioned elements.

@ Flexbox and Grid | I
Which property aligns flex items along the main axis?
= justify-content
- align-items
- align-content
- flex-wrap
? justify-content works on the main axis. align-items works on the cross axis.

@ Flexbox and Grid | I
Which declaration turns an element into a flex container?
= display: flex
- flex: container
- layout: flex
- position: flex
? display: flex makes the direct children flex items.

@ Flexbox and Grid | A
Which declaration creates three equal-width columns in CSS Grid?
= grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr)
- grid-columns: 3
- columns: 3fr
- grid-template: 3
? repeat(3, 1fr) creates three columns that share the available space equally.

@ Responsive Design | I
Which meta tag is essential for responsive pages on mobile devices?
= <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
- <meta name="mobile" content="true">
- <meta charset="responsive">
- <meta name="layout" content="fluid">
? The viewport meta tag tells mobile browsers to use the device width instead of a zoomed-out desktop layout.

@ Responsive Design | I
Which CSS feature applies styles depending on the screen width?
= Media queries
- Pseudo-elements
- CSS variables
- Keyframes
? @media (max-width: 600px) { ... } applies rules only on small screens.
